--TEST--
`?->` on a `null` receiver evaluates neither the member nor its arguments, counted over a sweep, and a `!= null` test narrows the receiver so plain `->` compiles inside the branch — `rule:types/narrowing`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:classes/nullable-objects-and
// The sibling short-circuit case passes a literal argument, which cannot tell an
// unevaluated argument from an evaluated one. Here every argument is a call that
// counts itself, so an argument the short-circuit failed to skip is visible in
// the tally rather than in the line it printed.
//
// `rule:types/narrowing`: the null test is branch-local, so `->` compiles inside
// the branch and the nullable spelling is still required outside it.

final class Tally {
    public static int $calls = 0;

    public static function next(int $n): int {
        Tally::$calls = Tally::$calls + 1;
        return $n;
    }
}

class Box {
    public function constructor(public string $label) {}

    public function grownBy(int $by): string {
        return $this->label . $by;
    }
}

?Box $some = new Box("here");
?Box $none = null;

// The present arm reaches the member, so its argument is evaluated once.
?string $answer = $some?->grownBy(Tally::next(1));
echo $answer ?? "gone", " calls=", Tally::$calls, "\n";

// The `null` arm reaches nothing, so the tally does not move.
$answer = $none?->grownBy(Tally::next(2));
echo $answer ?? "gone", " calls=", Tally::$calls, "\n";

// The agreement, counted rather than read off one line: ten short-circuits in a
// row add nothing at all, and ten present arms add exactly ten.
int $i = 0;
for (; $i < 10; $i = $i + 1) {
    $answer = $none?->grownBy(Tally::next($i));
}
echo "after ten short circuits calls=", Tally::$calls, "\n";

$i = 0;
for (; $i < 10; $i = $i + 1) {
    $answer = $some?->grownBy(Tally::next($i));
}
echo "after ten present arms calls=", Tally::$calls, "\n";

// `rule:types/narrowing`: inside the branch the receiver is no longer nullable,
// so plain `->` compiles there. The branch on the `null` value is not entered.
if ($none != null) {
    echo "unreachable=", $none->label, "\n";
}
if ($some != null) {
    echo "narrowed=", $some->label, "\n";
}

// Outside the branch it is nullable again, so `?->` is what reaches it.
echo "outside=", $some?->label ?? "gone", "\n";
--EXPECT--
here1 calls=1
gone calls=1
after ten short circuits calls=1
after ten present arms calls=11
narrowed=here
outside=here
